1
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and try stepping back,
will you?

2
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to me.

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,980
I've got none either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:36,300
white clouds.

6
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:42,820
Somehow, it'll all work out.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,560
I've got none either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,800
Super Io Change Lemon

10
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:53,680
It only just started spinning,
and it's already this popular

11
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:57,920
Even outside meal times,
there's a line this long.

12
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:00,980
Thank you for the meal.

13
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,180
Finally, it's our turn.

14
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:08,760
Mm.

15
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:17,520
What'll you have, senpai? We just got paid,
so let's splurge for once. Chashu ramen it is.

16
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:23,580
I'll have the same. Hey, old man, two chashu ramen.
Are your eyes just for show?

17
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:27,280
Can't you see the menu on the wall?
The menu!

18
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:29,360
Mm.

19
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:36,840
We only do ramen, though.
Just go sit somewhere else.

20
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:44,420
Wait, if the menu only has ramen, that means they're
really confident in their taste, right, senpai?

21
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:50,200
Well, maybe, but isn't that exciting either way?
Two ramen, please.

22
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,770
Hold on! We're customers!

23
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:02,920
At the very least, you should say "Welcome!"

24
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:06,840
We don't sell service here. We sell flavor.

25
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,980
If you don't like it, get out.

26
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,240
What did you say?!

27
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:15,000
Senpai, we lined up for this,
so please wait until we've eaten.

28
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,100
If it tastes bad,
you won't walk out of here for free!

29
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:20,700
If it tastes bad, you say?

30
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:23,320
Hey! We put our lives into Koshisora ramen!

31
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,199
Putting on a face like you
can't taste anything at all,

32
00:03:26,249 --> 00:03:27,740
Don't talk like you know everything!

33
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:32,080
Ramen like this isn't for cocky customers like you.
Get out already!

34
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:35,440
Yo! Hairy as can be,
cat hair and ash everywhere!

35
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,940
We don't want a shop like this!
We're out of here!

36
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,700
What?!

37
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,260
Honda, let's go!

38
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,820
S-s-s-senpai!

39
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,080
Hey! Throw salt, salt!

40
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:50,580
Finally, it's time.

41
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:54,520
I won't lose!
I put all my skill into making it today.

42
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:58,100
I got up at five in the morning for this day too,
you know.

43
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,880
Senior Kamachi, what's wrong? You seem down.

44
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:03,660
N-no, that's not true.

45
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,840
You didn't go and forget to make it,
did you?

46
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:10,800
O-of course not, I'm all set.

47
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:13,720
You! Take the king!

48
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,980
Oh my, Sei-senpai, wait, take that back!

49
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:19,780
I'm in a bad mood today
because of that cocky ramen shop.

50
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:20,860
Taking that back

51
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,160
Shatranj!

52
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,660
Hurry up and get your king out of there!

53
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,280
Move over, would you?

54
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,600
Why should I have to move?

55
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,720
Whoever grabs the seat first wins.

56
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,600
That seat is reserved.

57
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:35,280
Reserved?
It's not like this is a restaurant.

58
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,340
...right?

59
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:47,040
Sorry we're late. Welcome! We reserved this table,
but Kankichi keeps getting in the way. Don't make it beer.

60
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:59,260
We started something called a homemade lunch meeting.
Since we're so busy with work and can't cook much, once a month

61
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:07,240
we make an effort to pack lunches. Today's the first one,
so we were all going to critique each other's.

62
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:12,720
Not bad for you lot. Well, if that's
how it is, I guess it can't be helped.

63
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:16,460
Sorry about that.
Okay, everyone, here we go!

64
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:24,340
What's wrong, Matoi-chan? Did you forget?

65
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,480
Heh heh, that's what you say, anyway.

66
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,240
Didn't you forget on purpose
because you weren't confident?

67
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,120
S-senpai!

68
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:31,480
Yeah.

69
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,860
Don't say such irresponsible things!

70
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,200
Just like you, Matoi-chan.

71
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:42,000
Mokusei-san,
there's a kindergartner here asking for you.

72
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,240
A kindergartner?

73
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,060
Matoi, you bastard!

74
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,120
Huh?

75
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,400
Are you okay, senpai?

76
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:52,380
But

77
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,240
It's Lemon, after all.

78
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:55,960
So cute.

79
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,620
Mato-chan, do you know her?

80
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:58,820
I'm Lemon, her little sister.

81
00:05:58,820 --> 00:05:59,800
She's your sister?

82
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:00,900
So cute.

83
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,900
What's wrong, Lemon?

84
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,160
You came to bring my lunch.

85
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,600
Thanks, Lemon.

86
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,280
What's that little thing?

87
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:12,000
She's my sister. Didn't you know?

88
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,780
No, I never heard about her
when I was training under Gepard.

89
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:19,520
She was studying abroad in France back then.

90
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,340
Wait, studying abroad at her age?

91
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:23,480
Lemon's a genius when it comes to taste.

92
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:28,760
Mom says she has a palate that comes
along once in ten or a hundred years.

93
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,900
That's amazing, isn't it.

94
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:37,000
They sent her abroad just so she could eat
French food at a genuine three-star restaurant.

95
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,800
W-what?
They sent her to France just for that?

96
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,400
Geez, what is Gepard thinking?

97
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:49,200
Are you the worst of the Ryotsu men I've heard about,
Kankichi Ryotsu?

98
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,240
W-what did you say?

99
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:54,460
Not only are you a genius at taste,
you're a genius at judging people too

100
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:54,940
Shut up!

101
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:57,720
Your face and the way
you talk are both vulgar.

102
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:01,500
Wow... and mind your own business!

103
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:05,080
What's with that tone?
Did Gepard teach you that?

104
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:08,580
A kindergartener couldn't possibly
understand my good qualities.

105
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:12,000
That must have been quite a shock,
since it's the truth.

106
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,760
Against a senior officer,
she's basically a kindergartener.

107
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:18,660
Shut up!
I hate cocky brats like this the most.

108
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,440
Can you really tell the taste of food?

109
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,600
Interesting!

110
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:28,140
We were just about to hold a
homemade bento tasting contest!

111
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,760
Let's have you be the judge, then!

112
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,020
Sure, I guess.

113
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:32,660
Alright!

114
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,560
Shogi

115
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,220
What, you know how to play shogi?

116
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,240
A little.

117
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:44,560
What an irritating brat.

118
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,200
Hmm.

119
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,140
Your move, then. This side.

120
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:50,980
Whose turn is it?

121
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,600
Here, it's me.

122
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,680
My win isn't going to change, you know.

123
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,160
So you're the one winning

124
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,700
After all, you're just a kid.

125
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:03,420
I've taken your rook and bishop, you know!

126
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:05,780
How could you possibly say I'd lose?

127
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,920
It's an easy 33-move checkmate.

128
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,380
33 moves?

129
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,460
Don't talk nonsense.

130
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:13,900
If you could read that far ahead,
you'd be a pro.

131
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:14,980
Sorry.

132
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,680
Admitting you were lying,
you're surprisingly honest.

133
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:23,000
There was an even simpler 25-move checkmate.

134
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:26,220
W-what?

135
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:29,960
You little brat,
then let's see you checkmate me in 25 moves!

136
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:31,472
If you don't,

137
00:08:31,522 --> 00:08:34,180
I'm spanking your butt 100 times, got it?

138
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,520
Sexual harassment!

139
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,040
What a cheeky brat you are.

140
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:41,640
And if I do checkmate you,
what will Kankichi do for me?

141
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:43,340
Don't call me by my name
without the honorific!

142
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,300
Honestly, this kid makes my blood boil.

143
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:46,740
What'll you do, then?

144
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:50,980
I'll do a handstand in the buff
and walk around the whole shop.

145
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,320
Didn't you say you were going?

146
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:12,940
Lemon's the national kindergarten shogi champion,
you know.

147
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,180
As if that exists.

148
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,880
This is out of the question.

149
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:32,000
This is a makunouchi bento from Pokka Pokka-tei,
isn't it?

150
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,860
Come to think of it,
it's the same as my bento.

151
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:39,240
You just transferred it into a Yaikomachi bento box,
didn't you?

152
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,260
Is that so?

153
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:44,100
I overslept and didn't have time to make it.

154
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:44,940
*sigh*

155
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:48,460
Lemon, try my bento.

156
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:09,700
What's with this heavy tension?

157
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:11,280
And it's just acting, too.

158
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,120
How was it?

159
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:18,880
Today's in season, isn't it? Mebaru and
kanpachi are delicious this time of year too.

160
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:21,600
Ugh, what's with that
old geezer way of talking?

161
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,760
I'm not using such words, de gozaru.

162
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:27,400
That's it right there. You're saying
"de gozaru, de gozaro," aren't you?

163
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:31,600
Ryo-chan always watches period
dramas with his grandma, so.

164
00:10:31,650 --> 00:10:33,420
Sometimes he ends up talking in weird ways.

165
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,580
So it's that old lady's fault.

166
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,620
Even though you're a kid,
you really know your stuff.

167
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:38,220
Really?

168
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:40,460
How about the simmered bamboo shoots?

169
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:51,840
I used first-stock bonito dashi
and made it quite carefully.

170
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,980
But the scum hasn't been skimmed enough.

171
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,820
What's with that
high-and-mighty way of talking?

172
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:00,220
Now, now.

173
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:03,640
It's a Yadaman-style bento, I see.

174
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:05,340
Busted.

175
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,500
What, is it a copycat?

176
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,540
And it's a bento from
a top-class restaurant.

177
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:11,800
Do bad things and you'll get found out someday,
you know.

178
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:14,040
Lemon, try mine too.

179
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,880
Even without tasting, the winner is clear.

180
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:21,520
Appearance, aroma,
necessary nutrition, and calories.

181
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:24,820
On overall balance, Matoi wins, I'd say.

182
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:32,600
Say what you will, but letting your big sister's
bento win the top prize is still so childish of you.

183
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:37,540
Right? No matter how you look at it,
I think Reiko-san's bento is the best.

184
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:39,780
What, Reiko entered one too?

185
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:43,380
Well, the more entries the
better for these things, right?

186
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:44,440
Let's see, let's see.

187
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,740
This is a bento?

188
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:51,300
Seriously, foie gras sauté with caviar and truffle,
the ultra-deluxe version!

189
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:54,100
Admittedly, on ingredients alone,
it's the best.

190
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:57,360
But the way it's cooked is bad.

191
00:11:57,360 --> 00:12:00,980
When it's cooked this much,
you lose the original flavor.

192
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:06,520
The caviar here is too salty,
because it was put in straight from the can.

193
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,920
It could use a bit more work,
don't you think?

194
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:12,720
Being able to tell just by looking and smelling,
you really are a genius of taste.

195
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:14,060
Amazing, Lemon-chan.

196
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:17,260
You're really that amazing,
even though you're just a kindergartener?

197
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:22,700
That's it, I've got a good idea!

198
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:26,280
Hey, Matoi, lend me Lemon for about an hour.

199
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:28,440
Where do you plan to take her?

200
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:29,860
Come on, it's fine, right?

201
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:32,840
Sorry, but I'm heading home now.
I've left Sanpei waiting.

202
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,020
Alright, I'll go and sort it out with them.

203
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:40,260
There they are!

204
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,500
Hey, Ichiro-san.

205
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,420
This is bad.

206
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:52,980
She's on her way back from kindergarten,
so we need to contact the missus.

207
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:54,660
Right, I'll do the talking.

208
00:12:58,720 --> 00:12:59,860
Gepard.

209
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:01,740
What, it's Kankichi?

210
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,600
Shut up, don't call me by my name like that!

211
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:06,700
Hey, you, you look lame,
your ears are still sticking out.

212
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:07,920
What do you want?

213
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:10,360
I'm borrowing Lemon for an hour, all right?

214
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:13,560
What do you think you're
doing with our precious egg?

215
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:14,720
See ya.

216
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,760
As stubborn as ever, that old lady.

217
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,680
You can go home now.

218
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,200
Alright, let's go in hard!

219
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:46,500
I'd like you to taste something for me.

220
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:47,880
It's the ramen here, though.

221
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,580
Do you know a thing or two about ramen?

222
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:52,120
Of course,
from Asahikawa and Sapporo in the north

223
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,020
all the way down to Hakata
and Kumamoto in the south.

224
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:55,680
I'm well versed in ramen, too.

225
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:58,860
So stop talking so high and mighty.

226
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:02,240
You're a kid, so you should talk
in a more charming, childlike way.

227
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,400
Like saying
"how splendid" the way grandpa does.

228
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,860
Or saying things like
"Lemon-chan, you're so cute."

229
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,360
How eerie, isn't it?

230
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:11,160
Because it's not cute at all.

231
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,160
It's you again.

232
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,840
Came back for more

233
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,640
Now, don't get so worked up.

234
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,100
I've got no ramen to feed you.

235
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:22,840
Get lost for a while!

236
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:25,180
And don't you dare eat it this time!

237
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:26,560
This is the one.

238
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:29,940
This Lemon isn't just some kindergartner.

239
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:32,400
She has a palate that comes
once in a thousand years.

240
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:35,020
She's a super kindergartner, so to speak.

241
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,840
It's too dazzling,
you can't pull off a smooth act like that.

242
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:37,620
Stop playing to the crowd!

243
00:14:38,756 --> 00:14:43,220
Don't talk so high and mighty.

244
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:45,213
A taste-deaf sidekick like you,

245
00:14:45,263 --> 00:14:47,580
how could you possibly
understand the taste of my ramen?

246
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:48,400
Hurry up and go.

247
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,120
Wh-why?

248
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,340
Pork bones,
and the carcass of local free-range chicken,

249
00:14:57,340 --> 00:15:00,138
with green onion and
ginger to remove the odor,

250
00:15:00,188 --> 00:15:02,160
and maybe a little dried baby
sardine as a secret ingredient?

251
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:03,760
She's right!

252
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:07,490
Nyahahaha, I told you so.
Lemon is a genius of taste.

253
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:10,620
Now that you know,
hurry up and make the ramen, damn it.

254
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:12,480
A half bowl will do.

255
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:17,900
Here you go.

256
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,040
Eeeeeeeh!

257
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:39,400
*Grabs chopsticks*

258
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,100
Mm.

259
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:40,460
Mm.

260
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:00,920
What is this heavy tension?

261
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:02,760
She's just a kindergartener, yet...

262
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:09,640
The carefully grilled...
and this clear broth.

263
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,700
You've done quite good work.

264
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,400
How about the noodles?

265
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,980
This curl is exquisite.

266
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:23,480
It blends well with the soup.

267
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:26,040
You know your stuff, little lady.

268
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,300
Is the chashu Kagoshima black pork?

269
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:29,620
Yes.

270
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:32,360
Both the grilling and the
simmering get a passing grade.

271
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:37,560
Hey, our ramen is the best in Japan,
you know.

272
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,140
So, what do you think, Lemon?

273
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:43,860
It's so-so, I suppose.

274
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:46,320
So-so, you say?

275
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:48,365
It's certainly passing-grade flavor, but

276
00:16:48,415 --> 00:16:51,780
as long as you keep calling yourself the best in Japan,
you've still got a long way to go.

277
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:52,460
What?

278
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:56,700
The moment you convince yourself of something,
this ramen's flavor has stopped progressing.

279
00:16:57,960 --> 00:17:01,600
Flavor is something you refine through daily effort,
constantly raising it higher.

280
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,980
The moment you think
"this is good enough," it's over.

281
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:08,920
Don't you dare spout that borrowed nonsense,
you brat, like some know-it-all kid.

282
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:13,080
Then let me be specific:
the flaw in this ramen is the soy sauce.

283
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,760
Soy sauce?
Sorry, little lady, but you're wrong.

284
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:18,720
I stormed into the soy
sauce maker in Noda myself

285
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,980
and had them blend a custom batch for us.

286
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,420
There's no way it could be bad.

287
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:25,820
The maker is definitely
Umai soy sauce, right?

288
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:27,256
Y-yeah, but

289
00:17:27,306 --> 00:17:30,280
you can tell just from tasting the soup?

290
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,571
They changed presidents last year,

291
00:17:32,621 --> 00:17:35,500
and until then they used
100% domestic soybeans,

292
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:38,404
but now they use 20% foreign soybeans.

293
00:17:38,454 --> 00:17:40,540
The flavor has gone downhill.

294
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:42,100
Really?

295
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:46,260
Getting cocky and unable to check that much...
you've still got a long way to go.

296
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:49,120
My apologies for underestimating you.

297
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,400
Yes!

298
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:53,180
Lemon, you came through!

299
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:03,440
Never has my popularity
dropped this much in one day.

300
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:05,840
Lemon, you really are the greatest!

301
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:08,440
Kankichi, you're acting way
too excited for a grown man.

302
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:12,500
When you're happy or sad,
grown-ups and kids are no different.

303
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:17,500
I'm home.

304
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,180
Welcome back.

305
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,080
Kankichi-san, welcome.

306
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,900
Young mistress, it's been a while.

307
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:27,240
Grandma was so worried about you.

308
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:32,500
It's fine.
That old hag needs to worry a little.

309
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:35,960
Ryotsu, Kankichi, I'll take
responsibility and return Lemon to you.

310
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,660
Well then, I'll be going.

311
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,120
What's wrong, Lemon?

312
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:45,460
Mom, Lemon's shoes that
were kept here are gone.

313
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:47,480
Lemon's shoes?

314
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:50,820
The ones with the picture on them.

315
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,645
Those were dirty, and

316
00:18:54,695 --> 00:18:57,740
they'd gotten too small to wear,
so I threw them out earlier.

317
00:18:57,740 --> 00:19:00,380
That's awful,
I threw them away so carefully.

318
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:02,840
Carefully...

319
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:09,371
Those shoes, after Matoi joined the police,

320
00:19:09,421 --> 00:19:12,920
he bought them with his very first paycheck.

321
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:15,650
L-Lemon, you don't have to cry like that,

322
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,100
that's right, I'll buy you the same ones.

323
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:50,880
That garbage truck from earlier

324
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:53,680
It has to be.

325
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:56,960
It's okay.
We'll get them back, no matter what.

326
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:59,680
There's a bicycle in Honjo!

327
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,460
Lemon, get on the back.

328
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,820
Put this on and hold on tight.

329
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:06,900
Let's go!

330
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,260
Ichiro-san!

331
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,420
Please let us make it in time.

332
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:20,120
Hey! Stop!

333
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:24,500
That's the truck that collected
Kanda Sushi's garbage today, right!

334
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:28,880
But by now it's probably
all ash in the incinerator.

335
00:20:31,760 --> 00:20:33,500
It's okay, Lemon! Don't lose hope!

336
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:35,500
We'll definitely make it work somehow!

337
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:51,260
Hey!

338
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:55,240
Where's the garbage from
the sanitation truck?

339
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,000
Then it's over there.

340
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,140
Kankichi!

341
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,520
It's dangerous, so stay right there.

342
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:06,120
What color are the shoes?

343
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:08,360
Pink, pink!

344
00:21:08,360 --> 00:21:10,540
Got it, pink.

345
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:11,980
Here I go!

346
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:24,460
Pink, pink!

347
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:30,640
Pink, pink!

348
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:35,320
Pink, pink!

349
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:36,920
Found it, found it!

350
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,680
Kankichi!

351
00:21:49,260 --> 00:21:49,940
Alright!

352
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:55,680
Hey, you little punk! Let go!

353
00:21:55,900 --> 00:21:56,640
Nooo!

354
00:22:13,860 --> 00:22:14,860
Thank you, Kankichi.

355
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:16,900
For what?

356
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,540
Lemon's shoes.

357
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:19,900
What are you talking about?

358
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:22,120
You found them yourself, didn't you?

359
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:23,940
I just picked them up.

360
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:31,200
Lekki Part! What's that sword?

361
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:33,180
No arguments!

362
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:37,620
Hey, Kankichi!
Dragging Lemon around this late at night!

363
00:22:37,620 --> 00:22:38,380
How rude!

364
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,880
What happened to my bicycle?

365
00:22:41,020 --> 00:22:44,000
That one broke,
so I left it at the incinerator.

366
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,200
It's probably turned to ash by now.

367
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:48,000
Whaaat!

368
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:48,960
Good luck.

369
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:52,300
Kankichi-san, bicycles are oversized trash.

370
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:53,420
I see.

371
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,200
Thank you for taking care of Lemon.

372
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:56,580
Well, no.

373
00:22:57,020 --> 00:22:58,220
Do you like talking?

374
00:22:58,360 --> 00:22:59,780
I-it's a misunderstanding, I'm telling you!

375
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:01,137
Shut up.

376
00:23:01,187 --> 00:23:04,880
I'll make you rust on
the blade of Seki Magoroku.

377
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:06,620
Granny, that's not it.

378
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,560
It's okay, Lemon.

379
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,400
Matoi.

380
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:12,820
For those two, it's like a sport.

381
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,680
S-stop it!

382
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:18,340
You really cherished those shoes that much.

383
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:21,000
No, no, I said no!

384
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:21,780
Thank you.

385
00:23:21,780 --> 00:23:22,080
Stop it.

386
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:29,460
Geez, that old lady's full of life.

387
00:23:29,460 --> 00:23:31,640
W-wait, Kankichi!

388
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:34,280
See ya, Lemon. That was fun.

389
00:23:35,020 --> 00:23:37,040
Thanks, Kankichi. Bye-bye!

390
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:41,680
I've never seen Lemon
laugh this brightly before.

391
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:46,680
No way, no way, Lemon! Whatever you do, don't
you dare develop feelings for a guy like Ryotsu!

392
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:49,820
But I had fun with Kankichi, you know.

393
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:52,180
Fun? Really?

394
00:23:52,360 --> 00:23:52,760
Yeah.

395
00:23:54,320 --> 00:23:56,820
Well, I suppose I'll let it slide for today.

396
00:23:56,820 --> 00:23:58,500
Thanks, Grandma.

397
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:20,280
That drowsy time right
after the rain stopped,

398
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:24,540
I walked on, looking back over my shoulder.

399
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:27,120
Led along by the hand of a kid,

400
00:24:28,180 --> 00:24:33,740
that strange feeling I had back then.

401
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:39,560
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

402
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:45,300
I tried walking only on the black ones.

403
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:53,460
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

404
00:24:54,580 --> 00:24:57,620
Not the politicians with
their self-important faces.

405
00:24:57,620 --> 00:25:00,940
Not the aunties who are a
thorn in your side, either.

406
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:06,520
Go on, turn that corner over there.

407
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,680
I can meet everyone, everyone!

408
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:12,920
Don't go!

409
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:16,380
That place has walls.

410
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:19,720
Well, I'm sure there are walls.

411
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:24,960
Everyone, come on over to our town!

412
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you.

413
00:25:31,020 --> 00:25:33,860
That old Volvo guy opened a ninja school.

414
00:25:33,860 --> 00:25:36,520
Who'd learn ninjutsu these days?

415
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:39,580
Wait, if that helps catch criminals...

416
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:43,140
then we just need to get it adopted as
one of the police martial arts, right?

417
00:25:43,140 --> 00:25:45,420
Next time, I'll teach ninjutsu.

418
00:25:45,840 --> 00:25:47,340
Nice to meet you, de gozaru.

419
00:25:47,340 --> 00:25:48,220
Nin-nin.

